@param _patternIndex: pattern index (0-based, real pattern list order)
@param _baselineIndex: baseline index on the pattern (0-based, same order as GetPatternBaselinePoints); pass -1 to trace every baseline of the pattern (-1 is the only accepted negative value — any other negative index fails). Punch-mark (cross-mark) entries in that index space are position markers, not traceable shapes — they are skipped, and passing a punch-mark index returns false
@note In a GUI session the 2D/3D views and related widgets are not refreshed automatically by this API.
@note The receiving pattern is decided by geometric containment of the traced lines (the core's FindParentPattern), not by _patternIndex — when patterns overlap in the 2D window, the internal shape can be created on a different pattern than the baseline's owner.
@note On trace failure the core shows a modal message box that this API cannot suppress — it can block a headless session.
@return true when at least one internal shape was created; false when the pattern/baseline is not found, the index is negative (other than -1), no baseline line is selectable, or the trace failed
"""

